 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Epidermal retinol dehydrogenase 2</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_SDR16C5_identity" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_Q8N3Y7" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">RDHE2_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">RDHE2</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">SDR16C5</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Retinal short-chain dehydrogenase reductase 2</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Short-chain dehydrogenase/reductase family 16C member 5</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">1.1.1.105</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">RDH-E2</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">retSDR2</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">EPHD-2</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">RDHE2_HUMAN Reviewed; 309 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference101017</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/XP_005251237</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ra.cs.uni-tuebingen.de/software/KEGGtranslator/EC111105.eref</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_195814</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Oxidoreductase with strong preference for NAD. Active inboth the oxidative and reductive directions. Oxidizes all-trans-retinol in all-trans-retinaldehyde. No activity was detected with11-cis-retinol or 11-cis-retinaldehyde as substrates with eitherNAD(+)/NADH or NADP(+)/NADPH. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:18926804}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=all-trans-retinol--[retinol-binding protein] + NAD(+) =all-trans-retinal--[retinol-binding protein] + H(+) + NADH;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:48488, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:14428, Rhea:RHEA-COMP:14430, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:17336,ChEBI:CHEBI:17898, ChEBI:CHEBI:57540, ChEBI:CHEBI:57945,ChEBI:CHEBI:83228; EC=1.1.1.105;PATHWAY: Cofactor metabolism; retinol metabolism.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Endoplasmic reticulum membrane{ECO:0000305}; Multi-pass membrane protein {ECO:0000305}.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;Name=1;IsoId=Q8N3Y7-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=Q8N3Y7-2; Sequence=VSP_028389;TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Detected in adult lung. Detected at low levelsin adult brain, heart, testis, placenta, cervix, pancreas, uterus,stomach, rectum, small intestine, colon, esophagus, thymus, skin,and skin keratinocyte. Expression is higher in psoriasis lesionsrelative to unaffected skin from psoriasis patients. Detected infetal kidney, skin and lung. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12372410}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the short-chain dehydrogenases/reductases(SDR) family. {ECO:0000305}.SEQUENCE CAUTION:Sequence=BAB71545.1; Type=Frameshift; Positions=226; Evidence={ECO:0000305}; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_Q8N3Y7_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_195814</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

